{"chapter": "cotangent", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "08PL", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$A \\to B$", "MATH_0002": "$B$", "MATH_0003": "$A$", "MATH_0004": "$\\epsilon : P_\\bullet \\to B$", "MATH_0005": "$$\nP_0 = A[B],\\quad P_1 = A[A[B]],\\quad \\ldots\n$$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{simplicial-example-polynomial-algebra-maps}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-standard-resolution}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:be78fa7130a9ef6ffc49063750f8206b7c08a00c251bff11803fb8a6890f3bfb", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d89dae870bab5f0749fe0c4516e6770769a1da88b83cfa327777d39a527f0dbe", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a ring map. The <TEXTITOPEN_0001>standard resolution of <MATH_0002> over <MATH_0003><TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nis the augmentation <MATH_0004> with terms\n<MATH_0005>\nand maps as constructed in\nSimplicial, Example <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3fbc9cc6197ec9e71f1a55d262d5f16958709c3902f417d16cf6d8c8b9b67236", "unit_id": "tag:08PM:statement"}
{"chapter": "cotangent", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "08PL", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4470b7a7eec02ec2cbae8435f2e50b0e7ec1e428ba8dfcf0f593734852962dfc", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIt will turn out that we can use the standard resolution\nto compute left derived functors in certain settings.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d1d429f43829febccdf3392677450894a01768a674ee620d92d5c3c361e081c7", "unit_id": "tag:08PL:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "cotangent", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "08PL", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$L_{B/A}$", "MATH_0002": "$A \\to B$", "MATH_0003": "$B$", "MATH_0004": "$B$", "MATH_0005": "$$\n\\Omega_{P_\\bullet/A} \\otimes_{P_\\bullet, \\epsilon} B\n$$", "MATH_0006": "$\\epsilon : P_\\bullet \\to B$", "MATH_0007": "$B$", "MATH_0008": "$A$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-cotangent-complex-ring-map}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9578057284a2cfc262ea1b63bf0893c31e6ca3853251c0a7724cc9ac6c35d788", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b930e5e6e32fe3407d7e28965ab67084ffac4399f5fcf9af3b04c06e3fd0f289", "source_text": "The <TEXTITOPEN_0001>cotangent complex<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> <MATH_0001> of a ring map <MATH_0002>\nis the complex of <MATH_0003>-modules associated to the simplicial <MATH_0004>-module\n<MATH_0005>\nwhere <MATH_0006> is the standard resolution\nof <MATH_0007> over <MATH_0008>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:42b0721b426f9df2124beb5b6f15e537b029d91d0bd626fea298038227958039", "unit_id": "tag:08PN:statement"}
{"chapter": "cotangent", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "08PL", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$L_{B/A}^{-n}$", "MATH_0002": "$-n$", "MATH_0003": "$B$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Omega_{P_n/A} \\otimes_{P_n, \\epsilon_n} B$", "MATH_0005": "$L_{B/A}^m = 0$", "MATH_0006": "$m > 0$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{simplicial-section-complexes}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:686acbf30e76e20396cc4b936e84f0ba597710489dcd7ae64c4a3c5194e2a41f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d46b185f41ede3388618a1a86086c6d78730bb53433015c75c58aa8797c2545a", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn Simplicial, Section <REF_0001> we associate a\nchain complex to a simplicial module, but here we work with cochain complexes.\nThus the term <MATH_0001> in degree <MATH_0002> is the <MATH_0003>-module\n<MATH_0004> and <MATH_0005>\nfor <MATH_0006>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3e7e9846498c167d60ff10605835de07566cd878a8634321ce43cd4877c25682", "unit_id": "tag:08PL:prose-0003"}
